cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Periodic Table of Sound"
abstract: "A periodic table of musical elements ordered by time octave Z, measured on real recordings, with a sound collider for predicted elements. This version adds the amplitude envelope as a validated Level element; element cards and a prediction scoreboard that counts only predictions written down before their test; beat labels tapped by a listener, which showed that a single beat-level rule cannot be chosen; the metrical ladder, which reports every level of the pulse instead of one beat; pre-registered predictions for live recordings; the sidechain pump and a noise control in the collider; a calibrated false-alarm rate for period confirmation (a surrogate p-value) with exact intervals on every counted rate; and a negative pilot result on finding seams in generated audio. The research and the code were developed with Claude (Anthropic), an AI model."
authors:
